@Variable property list
Each screen and board can have a variable property list of up to 255
variable properties. Each one can be one of the following types:

þ Font: Load the specified font when this board or screen is entered.

þ Palette: Load the specified palette when this board or screen is entered.

þ Video mode: Sets the video mode for this board or screen. In this way,
you can have some screens using 80 columns or 40 columns and some might
use SMZX mode while others do not.

þ Scroll: Set the initial scroll position, by specifying the board
coordinates of the view center. This is only meaningful in boards and not
in screens, and if it is specified then it will override the default
handling of centering at the player.

þ Window field specification: The specification of a field in a window;
this can be refered by the window definition. This is only meaningful for
screens, and is ignored if it appears in a board. A field specification can
have up to fourteen character cells.

þ Music: Load and play background music when this board or screen is
entered. You can specify the criteria for doing so.

þ Cancel music: Causes the background music to be stopped when this board
or screen is entered. (This does not affect sound effects, and does not
affect any sounds played by SFX and #PLAY.)

þ Once: The previous variable property only applies once. This is only
meaningful for boards, and only if it persists; if the board does not
persist then it will not remember that it had already been done once.

Normally, the variable property list for the screen is applied first, and
then the variable property list for the board is applied and overrides the
specifications for the screen. However, for screens used as a text window
or other window, the screen's variable properties apply and override those
specified for the board.
